Thanks.  Mitzi just explained this pattern to me when I asked
her about command-line conventions! I had never noticed
before that single dashes had no equal signs and the double
dashes did.

Mitzi also said that the single dash often
had an abbreviated name, so it might be

    --lines=5

vs.

    -l 5

> Since command-line Stan is disproportionally used by people who do things via the command-line,

Linux integration == more command-line users

Python, MATLAB integration == fewer command-line users

Machine learning "marketing" == more command-line users

:-)

 > I think we should stick
