My only concern with the dashes is what to do for the categorical arguments.  For example, this is fine

./model sample --algorithm=hmc

but what about the "adapt" argument:

./model sample --algorithm=hmc adapt --engage=true

or

./model sample --algorithm=hmc --adapt --engage=true

adapt isn't a key/value pair so doesn't fit into the usual use-case, but giving it a different prefix breaks the symmetry amongst arguments.

Technically adding the prefix is easy -- honestly it's probably easiest to just strip away the prefix and use the current code.  Requiring a prefix is slightly more involved but still straightforward.

