and hence provides a bit of a learning curve.  So
and I'm not sure this is where we want to innovate.

I prefer the trailing colon to nothing as it distinguishes the
categorical features from the flags and indicates their scope.
I don't like the brackets.

What we probably really need is some kind of config file.
I took a quick poll.   I hate config files, Mitzi loves them :-)

I personally find this:

    --adapt_mu=5 --adapt_eta=8 --adapt_t0=2

easier to understand than this:

    adapt: mu=5 eta=8 t0=2

What do others think here?  I could be convinced to innovate
on the command line.  Someone has to do it some time.

I'm strongly opposed to having multiple ways of doing things.
The problem is that it bloats the doc size and also splits
all the help threads and examples.

