Let say I have a model

parameters {
  real mu_1;
  real mu_2;
}

transformed_parameters {
  real mu_a;
  real mu_b;

  mu_a = some_crazy_combo_of(mu_1, mu_2);
  mu_b = some_other_combo_of(mu_1, mu_2);

}

model {
  // likelihood
  mu_a ~ prior_dist();
  mu_b ~ prior_dist();
}

Will the Jacobian between (mu_1, mu_2) and (mu_a, mu_b) be added to the log_posterior?

