> Wouldn't we assume that all parameters are accessible in each block?

That would make sense.  And all the data and transformed data.

> As for constants and temps, why wouldn't we just treat the blocks as separate scopes?

That's simplest, but it prevents sharing local variables across
blocks.  And it forces all the transformed parameters to be computed
for each block if you want to also include those.

