It's bad, but there is not a whole lot I can do about it. When

1. There are a lot of new commits
2. The rebaser is not familiar with the commits
3. The develop branch has been pulled into the feature branch

then it is pretty much impossible to rebase explicitly.

What can be done is to create a patch of feature/arg_refactor against develop (at the time it was branched) and save that somewhere. Then make a new branch, git apply the patch, and commit hunks of it (perhaps using the --interactive option to git-add or git-gui). Then we merge the newest branch only.

Ben

